      {
        "case_id": "gp005",
        "category": "golden",
        "question": "How does the RAG retriever obtain documents for a query?",
        "answer": "- The retriever uses a **bi‑encoder** architecture: a BERT‑BASE query encoder q(x) produces a dense query vector, and a BERT‑BASE document encoder d(z) produces dense vectors for each document z . [chunk_1]\n- Document vectors are stored in a **non‑parametric memory** (the document index) built from Wikipedia chunks; the index is created with FAISS using a Hierarchical Navigable Small World (HNSW) approximation for fast similarity search . [chunk_3]\n- At inference, the query vector is compared to all document vectors with **Maximum Inner Product Search (MIPS)**; the top‑k documents with the highest inner‑product scores are retrieved as the candidate set . [chunk_1]",
